  "result": "The connected document-start disabled cancelSeq=4 -> enabled cancelSeq=5 sequence did not pause in any of three tested import/poll orderings. The explicit later disable positive control did set pendingPause and opened the original pause menu after unchanged warmup.",
  "observations": [
    "All four cases use actual original Windows bridge, shared input reducer, Backroad input adapter and StageMenus; connected ID/session stay identical; nine held buttons are false and A counter stays 7.",
    "Disabled seed includes wifiController.inputEnabled=false; enable includes true. Seed runs before any game PureGame callback exists.",
    "Three orderings: enable before game import, same JavaScript task after import before any RAF poll, and after first disconnected polls.",
    "No START/retry/resume input, clock override, physics model or renderer loaded. Chromium GPU/WebGL disabled. Original wall-clock RAF and original warmup constants remain.",
    "Both original Windows cases have no native suspend-script event and no inactive foreground trace. Native cancelSeq increase 3->5 is accounted for by navigation disable plus enable; it is not evidence of another cancellation.",
    "Original reports lack JavaScript blur/visibility/focus/networkChanged event history and first-controller sample history, so the actual native pause cause remains unproven."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Isolated DOM/bridge reproduction is not Windows COM/WebView2 or original TCP/native execution.",
    "No production or QA plan changed; native original failure remains failed.",
    "The known current test does not prove JS blur occurred. A bounded read-only actual browser event/cancellation trace would distinguish remaining callback paths."
